WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:05.690
In 1922, archaeologists dug into
a mound beside the Indus river.

2
00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:09.160
Beneath lay a city: Mohenjo-daro.

3
00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:10.390
Grid streets.

4
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:11.830
Covered drains.

5
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:13.700
A great brick pool.

6
00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:17.030
And thousands of small carved seals.

7
00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:19.440
Then the great cities shrank.

8
00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:23.350
Later came the Rig Veda:
hymns of fire sacrifice,

9
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.230
horses and chariots.

10
00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:28.620
Hinduism has no founder and no start date.

11
00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:32.180
So what can ruined cities
and old hymns tell us?

12
00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:34.690
In this mission, you'll examine the finds,

13
00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:37.420
from the Great Bath to clay figurines.

14
00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:41.460
Then you'll weigh up three rival accounts
of where the people of the hymns came

15
00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:42.280
from.

16
00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:47.050
Your mission: find out what ruined cities
and old hymns can tell us about how

17
00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.430
Hinduism began.
